# Multi-agent (Cursor)

**Default implementation agent: Builder** (`ilka-builder`). Switch role by task:

- **Architect** — unclear requirements, new module, ADR, API/DB contracts, tech choice
- **QA/Security** — after implementation, before merge, security bugs, production readiness
- **AI/CV** — cameras, video, models, inference, detection-to-event mapping

## Rules A–G

A. Inspect architecture docs and relevant files before edits.  
B. Small, reviewable changes.  
C. Meaningful tests with real behavior.  
D. No secrets in git or logs.  
E. Architecture/SoR/new service requires an ADR.  
F. Never call scaffold/mock **IMPLEMENTED**. Label `[MOCK / SYNTHETIC]`.  
G. Design for industrial reliability, security, observability, failure handling, maintainability, scale.

## Source of truth

`docs/PROJECT-OVERVIEW.md`, `REQUIREMENTS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `SYSTEM-ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CAMERA-ARCHITECTURE.md`, `AI-PIPELINE.md`, `EVENT-ARCHITECTURE.md`, `SECURITY-ARCHITECTURE.md`, `DATABASE-ARCHITECTURE.md`, `DEVELOPMENT-WORKFLOW.md`, `TESTING-STRATEGY.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `docs/DECISIONS/`. If they conflict: **stop** and request an ADR — do not guess.

## Handoff

Architect plan → Builder (one feature branch) → QA/Security → AI/CV if video/CV → Codex → Claude if needed → Builder fixes → QA → human merge.

Do not have two agents edit the same feature branch blindly. Reports for non-trivial work: `docs/agent-reports/`.
